WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:04.140
If you want to hear about the hidden text
on the computer screens and fourteen never

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:10.110
before revealed Things You Missed in Glass,
then stick around to the end of this video.

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:16.730
The first scene shows the birth of Elijah
Price, and we first see the child who would

00:00:16.730 --> 00:00:21.140
later become known as Mr. Glass, through the
reflection of a glass mirror.

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:25.180
This is a common theme in Unbreakable, we’re
introduced to age 13 Elijah through the reflection

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:29.250
of the Glass television screen, and we’re
introduced to Adult Elijah through the reflection

00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:31.890
of the glass in one of the pieces at his art
gallery.

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:35.409
When David meets Elijah for the first time,
not only are looking through a glass window,

00:00:35.409 --> 00:00:38.489
but the characters are framed in a box, just
like a comic book.

00:00:38.489 --> 00:00:39.809
"Here by appointment only."

00:00:39.809 --> 00:00:47.199
"I got a card from this store."

00:00:47.199 --> 00:00:50.840
The reason for these choices is that Elijah
sees himself as nothing more than a fragile,

00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:55.170
broken piece of Glass, and his entire purpose
throughout the film is to find his real place

00:00:55.170 --> 00:00:57.739
in the world, and discover why he is the way
he is.

00:00:57.739 --> 00:01:00.760
In the next scene we’re introduced to the
protagonist, David Dunn.

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:05.590
Note the alliteration of his name like many
other superheroes: Clark Kent, Peter Parker,

00:01:05.590 --> 00:01:07.720
Bruce Banner and several others.

00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:11.469
One of the first moments of David being on
screen has him looking at a child in the seat

00:01:11.469 --> 00:01:13.590
in front of him, who is upside-down.

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:17.420
Like the recurrent theme of glass, inversion
is also something that’s seen time and time

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:20.820
again in Unbreakable, and to understand it,
it’s important to understand the connection

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:23.210
between the film’s two central characters.

00:01:23.210 --> 00:01:26.369
David and Elijah are opposites in every way
but one.

00:01:26.369 --> 00:01:29.600
One is invincible, and the other of as fragile
as they come.

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:32.560
One gets sick very easily, the other is never
sick.

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:35.960
One is physically gifted, the other has a
hard time even getting around.

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:38.150
David is light skinned, Elijah has dark skin.

00:01:38.150 --> 00:01:41.130
David is very reserved, while Elijah is quite
outgoing.

00:01:41.130 --> 00:01:44.460
And of course, David is the hero, while Elijah
is the villain.

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:48.360
So when all is right with the world, the camera
is upright, as it should be.

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:53.021
But when disaster is about to strike… when
something bad is about to happen, the camera

00:01:53.021 --> 00:01:57.539
is inverted in relation to its subject, the
upside down girl precedes the train crash,

00:01:57.539 --> 00:02:01.659
David’s son Joseph watches TV upside-down
before learning of the crash, Elijah lays

00:02:01.659 --> 00:02:05.609
eyes on the comic book that first gives him
the idea that he’s a supposed to be a supervillain

00:02:05.609 --> 00:02:09.500
and it’s upside-down, Elijah falls down
the stairs and sees the man with the gun get

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:13.780
away with an inverted perspective and Joseph
sees his dad lift an impossible amount of

00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:17.590
weight from upside-down which later leads
him to pull a gun on his father.

00:02:17.590 --> 00:02:20.420
There’s also an inversion reference hidden
in the credits.

00:02:20.420 --> 00:02:24.310
David’s wife is named Audrey Dunn, but there’s
a separate credit for the actress who played

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:28.610
the age 20 Audrey before her and David were
married, where she’s referred to as Audrey

00:02:28.610 --> 00:02:29.610
Inverso.

00:02:29.610 --> 00:02:33.420
Finally, Elijah discovers a comic that helps
him find out what David’s kryptonite is

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:34.420
and that’s upside down as well.

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:40.210
Speaking of that kryptonite, that one weakness
that David has, David tells Kelly, the woman

00:02:40.210 --> 00:02:43.730
on the train, that he’s thinking about getting
into male synchronised swimming, which is

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:46.680
funny because we later find that his weakness
is water.

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:51.260
Director M Night Shyamalan also used the idea
of water as a weakness in his next film, Signs.

00:02:51.260 --> 00:02:54.760
There’s also a connection to his previous
film, The Sixth Sense, in that Bruce Willis

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:56.660
is the star of both movies.

00:02:56.660 --> 00:03:00.650
David’s wife also mentions that her favorite
song is Soft and Wet by the artist formerly

00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:02.560
known as Prince.

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:06.450
Another word for soft is weak, and David becomes
weaker whenever he gets wet.

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:10.400
Kelly also asks David if he likes football,
and he says, “not really”.

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:14.980
We later find out this is a lie, David was
a huge football star, and he still works as

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:18.820
a security guard at his former school’s
stadium so that he can continue to be around

00:03:18.820 --> 00:03:19.820
the game.

00:03:19.820 --> 00:03:23.540
Kelly is going to Philadelphia to meet with
a cornerback from Temple University, who later

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:27.540
appears in the movie, he’s in the park playing
football with a bunch of kids, one of which

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:33.250
is David’s son.

00:03:33.250 --> 00:03:35.900
Alright...

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:37.150
Always good to be back.

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:39.590
Now where were we?

00:03:39.590 --> 00:03:42.270
After the accident, Joseph is seen watching
television.

00:03:42.270 --> 00:03:45.660
I don't know how close they're gonna be able
to get David.

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:46.810
These are woods and trees.

00:03:46.810 --> 00:03:53.530
It's gonna be a very difficult rescue..."

00:03:53.530 --> 00:04:00.590
It starts with this Dole commercial featuring
a skateboarding Banana, then he flips the

00:04:00.590 --> 00:04:05.140
channel to Jerry Springer, then the Powerpuff
Girls, which is a 90s superhero cartoon, and

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:09.340
then an episode of I Am Weasel, another 90s
cartoon, this episode is about a smart banana

00:04:09.340 --> 00:04:12.010
that comes to life, it’s actually a really
funny episode.

00:04:12.010 --> 00:04:16.540
I’m not entirely sure why there are two
separate references to a living, sentient

00:04:16.540 --> 00:04:20.120
banana, perhaps an early foreshadowing of
The Horde, whose defining color is yellow.

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:22.910
Or perhaps something with Banana Split?

00:04:22.910 --> 00:04:24.280
Could be something there.

00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:28.990
I should also probably explain the color scheme
for anyone who hasn’t seen my Glass trailer

00:04:28.990 --> 00:04:29.990
analysis.

00:04:29.990 --> 00:04:34.270
David is almost always wearing Green, from
his shirt in scene two to his iconic rain

00:04:34.270 --> 00:04:35.270
poncho.

00:04:35.270 --> 00:04:38.780
Elijah can mostly be found wearing purple
and the present from his mother is wrapped

00:04:38.780 --> 00:04:39.780
in purple.

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:43.520
It even goes right down to Elijah’s purple
walled office and David’s kitchen with the

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:47.810
green cabinets, which looks beautiful when
complimented by the orange accents after David

00:04:47.810 --> 00:04:52.040
defeats the Orange man… oh man we could
talk about color theory all day with this

00:04:52.040 --> 00:04:55.060
movie, but let’s switch back to wherever
we were.

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:56.060
Right.

00:04:56.060 --> 00:04:57.060
The TV.

00:04:57.060 --> 00:05:00.680
The news of the train wreck comes in on channel
4 news, whose logo resembles the logo of the

00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:03.480
Marvel superhero group, the Fantastic Four.

00:05:03.480 --> 00:05:07.210
So David ends up being the only survivor of
the train crash , and after the memorial,

00:05:07.210 --> 00:05:12.020
receives a note from Elijah, which leads him
to discover he’s never actually been sick.

00:05:12.020 --> 00:05:15.720
Then we get the previously mentioned flashback
to Elijah’s childhood where he receives

00:05:15.720 --> 00:05:19.720
the gift from his mother, a comic book titled
The Battle With Jaguaro.

00:05:19.720 --> 00:05:24.420
Jaguaro is a beast like antagonist wearing
yellow and a reference to The Beast from Split.

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:28.610
Jaguaro is going up against a superhero wearing
green, obviously a reference to David.

00:05:28.610 --> 00:05:32.270
“They say this one has a surprise ending.”

00:05:32.270 --> 00:05:34.060
Yes, it does.

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:38.120
Elijah tries to sell the original artwork
as an adult, calling it a classic depiction

00:05:38.120 --> 00:05:39.530
of good vs. evil.

00:05:39.530 --> 00:05:43.510
However, when he learns that the buyer wants
to get this as a present for his kid, Elijah

00:05:43.510 --> 00:05:44.760
is outraged.

00:05:44.760 --> 00:05:48.331
I love that little moment where Elijah is
explaining that this is an art gallery, not

00:05:48.331 --> 00:05:52.180
a toy store, and he asks the prospective buyer,
do you see any Teletubbies in here?

00:05:52.180 --> 00:05:56.139
And the guy actually looks, like “oh my
God, there’s no teletubbies in here!”

00:05:56.139 --> 00:06:00.180
But anyway, after David meets Elijah, and
thinks he’s a scam artist, which is interesting

00:06:00.180 --> 00:06:04.310
in itself considering David’s innate ability
to sense evil, David goes home and reads the

00:06:04.310 --> 00:06:07.560
newspaper article about the train crash of
Eastrail 177.

00:06:07.560 --> 00:06:11.980
The photo of the wreck is credited to Kevin
Ladson, who’s actually the prop master for

00:06:11.980 --> 00:06:12.980
the movie.

00:06:12.980 --> 00:06:17.080
In the article, the name of the transportation
secretary is Kia Dickerson, who is also on

00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:18.230
the art department of Unbreakable.

00:06:18.230 --> 00:06:21.820
Part of the article mentions that the trains
had just had an engine check prior to leaving

00:06:21.820 --> 00:06:25.090
the station, an early hint that foul play
was involved.

00:06:25.090 --> 00:06:28.190
On the right column, there’s an article
about raising money to build prisons

00:06:28.190 --> 00:06:29.920
FOR YOU AND ME TO LIVE IN

00:06:29.920 --> 00:06:33.550
Excuse me, to house the number of inmates
expected in the next decade, perhaps some

00:06:33.550 --> 00:06:36.830
of the criminals caught by David Dunn will
inhabit these prisons.

00:06:36.830 --> 00:06:40.389
Then David takes a look back at the newspaper
highlights from his football career.

00:06:40.389 --> 00:06:44.389
One of the articles is written by Scott Murphy,
Shyamalan’s assistant art director, and

00:06:44.389 --> 00:06:48.660
the photographer Jim Feng is a reference to
James Feng, another assistant art director.

00:06:48.660 --> 00:06:52.300
Here’s another reason I love this movie,
always good to see the Brewers losing.

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:56.390
The article about David’s car crash in college
is written by Robert Holtzman, yet another

00:06:56.390 --> 00:06:57.680
assistant set decorator.

00:06:57.680 --> 00:07:01.610
He’s interrupted from reliving his glory
days when his wife comes knocking on his door

00:07:01.610 --> 00:07:05.100
asking if David has been with anyone since
they started having problems.

00:07:05.100 --> 00:07:07.880
“I’m prepared for any answer.

00:07:07.880 --> 00:07:10.180
It won’t affect me.”

00:07:10.180 --> 00:07:11.330
She’s lying.

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:14.210
“The answer won’t affect me.”

00:07:14.210 --> 00:07:15.360
She’s lying.

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:18.820
"It won’t affect me either way.”

00:07:18.820 --> 00:07:19.970
She’s lying.

00:07:19.970 --> 00:07:20.970
“No.”

00:07:20.970 --> 00:07:21.970
Told you.

00:07:21.970 --> 00:07:25.270
The next day at work, Elijah shows up and
we’re introduced to David’s ability to

00:07:25.270 --> 00:07:28.919
sense bad people in a crowd, when he predicts
that a man wearing camouflage is carrying

00:07:28.919 --> 00:07:33.169
a silver weapon with a black grip and that
will step out of line, which he does.

00:07:33.169 --> 00:07:35.199
Elijah sets out to see if David’s prediction
is correct.

00:07:35.199 --> 00:07:38.639
He steps out of his car which is completely
covered in padding, in order to pursue the

00:07:38.639 --> 00:07:42.490
guy, but on the stairs to the subway, has
a bad fall, and the shattering of his glass

00:07:42.490 --> 00:07:44.260
cane represents his frailty.

00:07:44.260 --> 00:07:47.620
I already talked about these scenes, so let’s
move onto the next stadium scene.

00:07:47.620 --> 00:07:51.520
A single mother in red bumps into him and
he heads the sounds of child abuse.

00:07:51.520 --> 00:07:57.840
Roll it like the spirit of Philadelphia.

00:07:57.840 --> 00:08:00.350
“No….”

00:08:00.350 --> 00:08:06.639
Maybe… just maybe… this kid is a young
Kevin Wendell Crumb from Split, but it might

00:08:06.639 --> 00:08:08.070
be impossible to know for sure.

00:08:08.070 --> 00:08:13.120
It is a different actress playing the Mom,
but it has been 15 years, so it's just possible

00:08:13.120 --> 00:08:16.630
that they weren't able to get that woman who
was an extra on set back to play the Mom.I

00:08:16.630 --> 00:08:17.630
don't know.

00:08:17.630 --> 00:08:19.430
Let me know what your thoughts on that are
in the comments though.

00:08:19.430 --> 00:08:22.710
Then there’s a cameo from the director M
Night Shyamalan himself.

00:08:22.710 --> 00:08:26.050
David is called away from work because his
son Joseph has an injury at school, when he

00:08:26.050 --> 00:08:30.210
gets in a fight with two kids, who we later
find out are Potter and some other guy.

00:08:30.210 --> 00:08:33.360
“It was Potter and another guy.

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:37.899
There were messing with this Chinese girl
in the dressing room.”

00:08:37.899 --> 00:08:40.779
You may remember Potter is the cousin of the
Cornerback from temple.

00:08:40.779 --> 00:08:42.579
“He’s Potter’s cousin.

00:08:42.579 --> 00:08:45.139
He’s starting cornerback at Temple University.”

00:08:45.139 --> 00:08:47.819
Then we’ve got Joseph’s gun scene.

00:08:47.819 --> 00:08:52.369
Now supposedly this was inspired by an incident
that really happened to Superman actor George

00:08:52.369 --> 00:08:56.380
Reeves, where a child confronted him with
a gun and asked to shoot him to prove Superman

00:08:56.380 --> 00:08:59.749
was invincible, and Reeves convinced him to
put the gun down by telling him that someone

00:08:59.749 --> 00:09:01.079
might be injured by the ricochet.

00:09:01.079 --> 00:09:05.100
I don’t know if that story is true, but
either way it could have been used as inspiration

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:06.510
for the Unbreakable scene.

00:09:06.510 --> 00:09:10.149
Finally, David revisits the wrecked train
cars and remembers the incident he and Audrey

00:09:10.149 --> 00:09:14.350
went through in college, where we has actually
completely unharmed in the car accident.

00:09:14.350 --> 00:09:17.730
He decides to become a vigilante, and saves
the two kids from the orange man.

00:09:17.730 --> 00:09:20.449
In the newspaper article that comes out the
next day we find out that those kids were

00:09:20.449 --> 00:09:22.939
tied up like that for 3 days.

00:09:22.939 --> 00:09:27.279
The author of the article, Nicole Marsella,
is of course an Art Department assistant.

00:09:27.279 --> 00:09:30.999
Scott Murphy, the sportswriter from before
also has something to say about the breaking

00:09:30.999 --> 00:09:35.899
up of farmland in this other article, so this
man has many passions it seems, and the farmland

00:09:35.899 --> 00:09:47.069
stuff could be another hint towards signs
being Shyamalan’s next film.

00:09:47.069 --> 00:09:57.740
Finally, David visits Elijah’s art gallery
showing and meets his mother.

00:09:57.740 --> 00:10:00.649
“See the villains eyes?

00:10:00.649 --> 00:10:04.491
They’re larger than the other characters.

00:10:04.491 --> 00:10:08.350
They insinuate a slightly skewed perspective
of how they see the world.”

00:10:08.350 --> 00:10:12.129
These are just a couple final clues towards
the reveal that’s about to happen in a couple

00:10:12.129 --> 00:10:13.129
minutes.

00:10:13.129 --> 00:10:16.860
Elijah has always seen the world from a skewed
perspective through those big eyes of his.

00:10:16.860 --> 00:10:18.689
But what’s truly amazing is her next comment.

00:10:18.689 --> 00:10:19.689
“But he says there’s always two kinds.

00:10:19.689 --> 00:10:31.290
There’s the soldier villain who fights the
hero with his hands… and then there’s

00:10:31.290 --> 00:10:33.920
the real threat, the brilliant and evil arch-enemy…
who fights the hero with his mind.”

00:10:33.920 --> 00:10:38.079
Shyamalan was planning to bring The Horde
from Split into the equation from the very

00:10:38.079 --> 00:10:39.079
beginning.

00:10:39.079 --> 00:10:42.540
In fact, he would later reveal that The Horde
was at one point supposed to be a part of

00:10:42.540 --> 00:10:45.839
Unbreakable, but he cut the character and
saved him for Split because the movie was

00:10:45.839 --> 00:10:46.980
getting too crowded.

00:10:46.980 --> 00:10:51.170
The final freeze frame of the movie states
Elijah Price is in an institution for the

00:10:51.170 --> 00:10:52.640
criminally insane.

00:10:52.640 --> 00:10:56.610
Why would is say that if this is not a true
story, and Shyamalan wasn’t planning on

00:10:56.610 --> 00:11:07.199
having Glass take place in that institution
19 years later?

00:11:07.199 --> 00:11:12.529
Both Split and Unbreakable open with a birthday
scene.

00:11:12.529 --> 00:11:16.649
In Unbreakable, it was the birth of Elijah
Price, and in Split, Claire Benoit celebrates

00:11:16.649 --> 00:11:17.649
her birthday.

00:11:17.649 --> 00:11:21.110
At the end of the party, her dad offers a
ride to her classmate, Casey Cooke, but he

00:11:21.110 --> 00:11:22.790
never quite makes it into the car.

00:11:22.790 --> 00:11:26.970
Last week, I described how David Dunn and
Elijah Price are color coded, with David being

00:11:26.970 --> 00:11:29.769
associated with green and Elijah being purple.

00:11:29.769 --> 00:11:32.050
The Horde has their own color too -- yellow.

00:11:32.050 --> 00:11:36.420
It can be seen in Dennis’s handkerchief,
Hedwig's jacket, the flowers placed around

00:11:36.420 --> 00:11:39.720
the holding room and at the train station,
the lighting and wall colors throughout the

00:11:39.720 --> 00:11:43.610
area below maintenance as well as the tiles
above ground at the zoo.

00:11:43.610 --> 00:11:46.860
In the poster for Glass, the colors of each
character are made clear.

00:11:46.860 --> 00:11:50.850
There are 24 sets of titles in the opening
and closing credits of Split, one for each

00:11:50.850 --> 00:11:52.769
of the 24 identities of The Horde.

00:11:52.769 --> 00:11:56.269
The opening credits also have letters connected
by a vertical line in a way that makes it

00:11:56.269 --> 00:12:00.779
look like two entries on a timeline, just
as this is the second entry in this series.

00:12:00.779 --> 00:12:05.319
The accompanying music by West Dylan Thordson
sounds like distorted animal cries.

00:12:05.319 --> 00:12:17.200
Take a listen.

00:12:17.200 --> 00:12:19.579
So the girls are kidnapped and put in this
holding room.

00:12:19.579 --> 00:12:23.100
Claire and Marcia have different ideas about
how to get out than Casey, and the room is

00:12:23.100 --> 00:12:27.649
vertically split, just like the title of the
movie, by this power line to show the divide.

00:12:27.649 --> 00:12:31.399
Vertical divisions of the frame are also a
technique used a lot in Alfred Hitchcock’s

00:12:31.399 --> 00:12:32.760
horror classic, Psycho.

00:12:32.760 --> 00:12:37.040
M Night Shyamalan, the director of Split,
lists Hitchcock as a huge influence, he even

00:12:37.040 --> 00:12:40.899
released a 10 minute video on his appreciation
of Hitchcock’s Strangers on a Train.

00:12:40.899 --> 00:12:44.750
There are other Psycho references in Split,
but we’ll get to them when we get to them.

00:12:44.750 --> 00:12:48.329
Casey tells Marcia to pee herself when Dennis
takes her out of the room -- hoping to prevent

00:12:48.329 --> 00:12:51.059
Dennis from forcing her to do something she
doesn’t want to do.

00:12:51.059 --> 00:12:54.560
The fact that Dennis is a germaphobe works
in her favor, but really, that was really

00:12:54.560 --> 00:12:55.560
just luck.

00:12:55.560 --> 00:12:59.019
Around this time, one of the other identities,
Barry, reaches out to their psychologist,

00:12:59.019 --> 00:13:00.019
Dr. Fletcher.

00:13:00.019 --> 00:13:02.189
She’s got several other emails on the screen.

00:13:02.189 --> 00:13:06.179
Just as the art department of Unbreakable
had cameos in the newspaper, the crew of Split

00:13:06.179 --> 00:13:08.309
makes cameos in Dr. Fletcher’s email.

00:13:08.309 --> 00:13:11.139
Charles S Rowe is credited as a miscellaneous
crew member.

00:13:11.139 --> 00:13:15.700
John B West, Dominic Catanzarite and John
Rusk were part of the production department.

00:13:15.700 --> 00:13:21.009
Mitch Campbell, Lucas Andrei, Jennifer Wessner,
Ed Mendez and Bob Lowery all worked visual

00:13:21.009 --> 00:13:22.009
effects.

00:13:22.009 --> 00:13:26.239
Skip Lievsay, Bryan Baker, Adam Leach and
Matthew Shapiro were part of the post production

00:13:26.239 --> 00:13:27.239
team.

00:13:27.239 --> 00:13:29.709
And Lisa Liberati is James McAvoy’s girlfriend.

00:13:29.709 --> 00:13:33.499
One of the emails mentions Cezanne, the French
painter, we’ll come back to that later.

00:13:33.499 --> 00:13:36.610
I love all these movies with just disturbing
pictures in the background.

00:13:36.610 --> 00:13:40.220
Anyway, Barry comes to see Dr. Fletcher, but
it’s not really Barry.

00:13:40.220 --> 00:13:43.829
Dr. Fletcher asks if he’s looking for something,
but he’s actually putting the room in order,

00:13:43.829 --> 00:13:46.230
because it’s really Dennis, the guy with
OCD.

00:13:46.230 --> 00:13:49.179
Imagine having a disorder within your disorder.

00:13:49.179 --> 00:13:50.800
Maybe Mr. Glass can relate.

00:13:50.800 --> 00:13:54.389
“I have something called osteogenesis imperfecta.

00:13:54.389 --> 00:13:56.600
It’s a genetic disorder.”

00:13:56.600 --> 00:14:00.019
"My name is Dr. Ellie Staple, and I'm a psychiatrist.

00:14:00.019 --> 00:14:07.120
I specialize in those individuals who believe
they are super heroes."

00:14:07.120 --> 00:14:12.040
Anyway, the supposed Barry talks about making
a jacket hand printed with newspaper headlines.

00:14:12.040 --> 00:14:16.339
“That’s supposed to be like a tailored
jacket, but I’m gonna handprint it with

00:14:16.339 --> 00:14:17.339
newspaper headlines.”

00:14:17.339 --> 00:14:21.179
I know someone who happens to have a collection
of newspaper headlines.

00:14:21.179 --> 00:14:24.579
Also in Dr. Fletcher’s office there’s
a picture on the wall of what appears to be

00:14:24.579 --> 00:14:28.819
a woman looking behind a shower curtain. this
is one of those Psycho references I was talking

00:14:28.819 --> 00:14:30.420
about.

00:14:30.420 --> 00:14:38.399
After Dennis leaves, Dr. Fletcher goes through
her patient files.

00:14:38.399 --> 00:14:41.980
The only one that’s legible is this one
on a Mr. Douglass Latreille.

00:14:41.980 --> 00:14:46.730
As far as I can tell, the name is not relevant,
but the dates on the file range from July

00:14:46.730 --> 00:14:48.649
2000 to November 2000.

00:14:48.649 --> 00:14:52.819
November 2000 is when Unbreakable was released,
and most of the movie is set within these

00:14:52.819 --> 00:14:56.440
dates, for example the encounter with The
Orange Man in Unbreakable takes place just

00:14:56.440 --> 00:14:57.929
before October 23rd 2000.

00:14:57.929 --> 00:15:00.610
She also has a bin labeled ‘Universal Offices’.

00:15:00.610 --> 00:15:04.440
You can probably guess who produced this movie.

00:15:04.440 --> 00:15:09.799
Dr. Fletcher visits an art gallery to view
this Cezanne painting, probably the one she

00:15:09.799 --> 00:15:11.170
received the email about.

00:15:11.170 --> 00:15:12.739
This piece is called the Bathers.

00:15:12.739 --> 00:15:16.949
Would it be too much of a stretch to relate
this to David Dunn’s swimming pool accident

00:15:16.949 --> 00:15:18.579
or fear of water?

00:15:18.579 --> 00:15:22.699
If your answer is yes, that is too much of
a stretch, then fine, but there’s no denying

00:15:22.699 --> 00:15:26.860
this line from Dr. Fletcher’s associate
Joe, was an intentional clue.

00:15:26.860 --> 00:15:32.089
“You treat them like they’re supernaturally
gifted, like they have powers or something.

00:15:32.089 --> 00:15:33.670
Karen, these are patients.

00:15:33.670 --> 00:15:35.639
They have been through trauma.”

00:15:35.639 --> 00:15:37.660
Whoa, that’s a good one.

00:15:37.660 --> 00:15:40.549
I’m curious if any of you picked up on that
the first time through, and at what point

00:15:40.549 --> 00:15:42.420
did you actually realize this was a sequel.

00:15:42.420 --> 00:15:46.359
I tried to look for some more clues in Dr.
Fletcher’s notes on the various identities,

00:15:46.359 --> 00:15:47.790
but I couldn’t really make out anything.

00:15:47.790 --> 00:15:51.290
I don’t know if this is supposed to be a
joke on that whole trope about doctors having

00:15:51.290 --> 00:16:02.320
bad handwriting, but I can’t read any of
it, so let’s go back to Casey and the girls.

00:16:02.320 --> 00:16:05.879
Casey awakes from a flashback and we see her
point of view which is sideways.

00:16:05.879 --> 00:16:09.619
When I talked about Unbreakable, I examined
the right-side-up vs upside-down shots in

00:16:09.619 --> 00:16:14.119
that movie, so maybe these sideways shots
in Split are a little bit of an in-between.

00:16:14.119 --> 00:16:17.819
This is also one of the first time we get
a good peek out of the holding room and there’s

00:16:17.819 --> 00:16:21.990
a container of Barnum Animal Crackers, one
of the earliest clues towards their location

00:16:21.990 --> 00:16:23.329
being the Philadelphia Zoo.

00:16:23.329 --> 00:16:27.570
“It took forever to get this place safe
without the nosy-bodys who work here finding

00:16:27.570 --> 00:16:28.570
out.

00:16:28.570 --> 00:16:29.629
You can’t get out of here!”

00:16:29.629 --> 00:16:33.739
Back at Dr. Fletcher’s office, we’ve got
our M Night cameo in the form of this guy

00:16:33.739 --> 00:16:37.459
who helps Dr. Fletcher review security camera
footage of Dennis deliberately trying to prove

00:16:37.459 --> 00:16:39.819
that he’s Barry by walking through the trash.

00:16:39.819 --> 00:16:43.250
When Patricia brings Casey and Marcia into
the kitchen, you can briefly see that they

00:16:43.250 --> 00:16:47.100
all have different cereal preferences, which
I found to be an interesting detail.

00:16:47.100 --> 00:16:50.519
One of the things I talked about in Unbreakable
is how we always see Elijah through a glass

00:16:50.519 --> 00:16:53.579
reflection to represent the fragile nature
of his disorder.

00:16:53.579 --> 00:16:57.189
We see Elijah though the a reflection each
time he is introduced at a new age.

00:16:57.189 --> 00:17:01.429
In Split, we see Dennis in the reflection
of this certificate just before he first introduces

00:17:01.429 --> 00:17:03.079
himself to Dr. Fletcher.

00:17:03.079 --> 00:17:06.880
There’s another reflection scene later on,
which I’ll come back to.

00:17:06.880 --> 00:17:11.299
But in this conversation, we find out that
the 24th identity, The Beast, resides away

00:17:11.299 --> 00:17:15.600
from the other 23 identities in a train yard,
because Kevin’s dad left on a train when

00:17:15.600 --> 00:17:18.839
he was young, presumably, that was Eastrail
177.

00:17:18.839 --> 00:17:22.730
Casey convinces Hedwig to show her his room,
which, in another clue about them being under

00:17:22.730 --> 00:17:25.500
the zoo, is filled with animal posters and
toys.

00:17:25.500 --> 00:17:29.740
Additionally the song that he famously dances
to in his room is called “Frogbass” by

00:17:29.740 --> 00:17:37.389
the artist currently known as Snails.

00:17:37.389 --> 00:17:51.480
And this is actually a pretty good drawing
of Reshiram if that’s what it’s supposed

00:17:51.480 --> 00:17:52.480
to be.

00:17:52.480 --> 00:17:55.500
Hedwig shows Casey the walkie talkie that
he stole from Dennis, and Casey uses it to

00:17:55.500 --> 00:17:58.870
try to call help, but the man on the other
end thinks that it’s just his friend pulling

00:17:58.870 --> 00:18:01.820
his leg and assures him he still has the orange
headphones.

00:18:01.820 --> 00:18:04.610
When Casey eventually does get out at the
end of the movie, we do see him listening

00:18:04.610 --> 00:18:06.929
to the orange headphones before he calls the
police.

00:18:06.929 --> 00:18:11.159
But, before any of that, there’s a very
important flashback where young Casey holds

00:18:11.159 --> 00:18:16.059
her abusive Uncle at gunpoint, in a scene
that’s very, very reminiscent of Joseph

00:18:16.059 --> 00:18:18.260
holding David at gunpoint in Unbreakable.

00:18:18.260 --> 00:18:19.600
Roll it.

00:18:19.600 --> 00:18:22.290
Split: “This isn’t funny.”

00:18:22.290 --> 00:18:28.429
Unbreakable: “Joseph what the hell are you
doing?”

00:18:28.429 --> 00:18:32.230
Split: “Is it loaded?”

00:18:32.230 --> 00:18:37.101
Unbreakable: “Joseph did you load that gun?”

00:18:37.101 --> 00:18:38.101
Split: “Casey”
Unbreakable: “Joseph.”

00:18:38.101 --> 00:18:39.101
Split: “I’m your Uncle.”

00:18:39.101 --> 00:18:40.101
Unbreakable: “Now I am your father…”

00:18:40.101 --> 00:18:41.101
Split: “Stop it Casey.”

00:18:41.101 --> 00:18:42.101
Unbreakable: “Joseph!”

00:18:42.101 --> 00:18:43.101
Split: “Put that gun down.”

00:18:43.101 --> 00:18:44.101
Unbreakable: “and I’m telling you to put
that ******* gun down right now!”

00:18:44.101 --> 00:18:45.101
Split: “I’m getting upset.

00:18:45.101 --> 00:18:46.101
I’m about to get very angry!”

00:18:46.101 --> 00:18:55.390
Unbreakable: “You are about to be in big
trouble!”

00:18:55.390 --> 00:19:13.490
Split: “You could have killed me.”

00:19:13.490 --> 00:19:17.409
These scenes take place at almost the exact
same point in both movies.

00:19:17.409 --> 00:19:21.080
Maybe one day I’ll do a side by side comparison,
but that sounds like another video.

00:19:21.080 --> 00:19:25.210
Dr. Fletcher’s concern leads her to try
to talk to The Horde at his home, so she pull

00:19:25.210 --> 00:19:26.210
up in a taxi.

00:19:26.210 --> 00:19:30.380
Remember how the Channel 4 news logo in Unbreakable
was very reminiscent of the Fantastic Four

00:19:30.380 --> 00:19:31.380
logo?

00:19:31.380 --> 00:19:35.450
Well the letter T in this taxi cab service
is also a reference to the Teen Titans logo.

00:19:35.450 --> 00:19:39.690
The pieces are all coming together as Dennis
visits the train station to transform into

00:19:39.690 --> 00:19:43.870
The Beast, and it’s an Amtrak train just
like Eastrail 177.

00:19:43.870 --> 00:19:47.970
Casey explores The Horde’s computer, and
this is where we see video diaries of each

00:19:47.970 --> 00:19:48.970
member.

00:19:48.970 --> 00:19:52.730
One of them is named Norma, which completes
the trifecta of Psycho references, this one

00:19:52.730 --> 00:19:54.510
referencing Norma Bates.

00:19:54.510 --> 00:19:58.580
At some point, Dr. Fletcher realizes she probably
won’t make it out alive, but she leaves

00:19:58.580 --> 00:20:00.230
a note for the captive girls to find.

00:20:00.230 --> 00:20:03.419
The note is written on a receipt from “Hagenbaugh
Laboratories”.

00:20:03.419 --> 00:20:04.780
Which is not a thing.

00:20:04.780 --> 00:20:08.610
BUT, Emily Hagenbaugh is the author of this
superhero book.

00:20:08.610 --> 00:20:12.580
So you know how the rest goes, Casey has her
confrontation with the Beast, the Beast sees

00:20:12.580 --> 00:20:16.179
that she too has gone through abuse and lets
her live.

00:20:16.179 --> 00:20:19.370
Someone finds her and escorts her from the
below maintenance area and the orange headphones

00:20:19.370 --> 00:20:20.710
guy calls the police.

00:20:20.710 --> 00:20:24.630
One of the most disturbing things to me, is
that even after all that Casey has been through,

00:20:24.630 --> 00:20:27.330
she still doesn’t want to go back with her
Uncle at the end.

00:20:27.330 --> 00:20:28.730
That’s how bad he is.

00:20:28.730 --> 00:20:32.220
But there’s one more loose end that still
hasn’t been tied up.

00:20:32.220 --> 00:20:33.220
On my end.

00:20:33.220 --> 00:20:36.820
I mentioned the Unbreakable reference where
we see The Horde in the reflection in Dr.

00:20:36.820 --> 00:20:39.540
Fletcher’s office, just like those Elijah
Price scenes from the first movie.

00:20:39.540 --> 00:20:43.840
The final scene with The Horde goes all in
on this, and includes the panning back and

00:20:43.840 --> 00:20:47.009
forth camera movement, as seen in many of
the scenes of Unbreakable.

00:20:47.009 --> 00:20:51.919
All the while James Newton Howard’s Unbreakable
soundtrack slowly transitions in as we cut

00:20:51.919 --> 00:20:56.500
to the credits and the iconic in-credit scene
and the reveal of David Dunn.

00:20:56.500 --> 00:20:59.380
I’ve got goosebumps just thinking about
it.

00:20:59.380 --> 00:21:10.929
Now the stage is set for Glass and I could
not be more excited.

00:21:10.929 --> 00:21:15.080
Glass begins with four cheerleaders abducted
by Hedwig and David Dunn, who is starting

00:21:15.080 --> 00:21:19.009
to become known as the Overseer, shifting
his focus from petty criminals to The Horde.

00:21:19.009 --> 00:21:23.059
We first see him take out these kids who are
filming themselves Superman punching a random

00:21:23.059 --> 00:21:25.289
guy on the street to try to go viral.

00:21:25.289 --> 00:21:29.360
These low criminals are pretending to be superheroes
online, which provides a stark contrast with

00:21:29.360 --> 00:21:32.889
the ending of Glass where real superheroes
leak on social media.

00:21:32.889 --> 00:21:37.160
When David first enters the house, he runs
water from a faucet, a strange choice considering

00:21:37.160 --> 00:21:42.890
water is his only weakness.

00:21:42.890 --> 00:21:47.750
"Who's there?"

00:21:47.750 --> 00:21:50.919
David now has his own security company, Dunn
Home Security.

00:21:50.919 --> 00:21:54.980
Elijah says in Unbreakable says that David
works in security for a reason, because he’s

00:21:54.980 --> 00:21:57.100
a born protector, so it makes sense that he
gets his own company.

00:21:57.100 --> 00:22:00.059
“You could have been a tax accountant.

00:22:00.059 --> 00:22:01.059
You could have owned your own gym.

00:22:01.059 --> 00:22:02.059
You could have opened a chain of restaurants.

00:22:02.059 --> 00:22:08.460
You could have done one of 10,000 things,
but in the end you chose to protect people.

00:22:08.460 --> 00:22:13.909
You made that decision, and I find that very,
very interesting.”

00:22:13.909 --> 00:22:17.180
Joseph keeps a list of quotes said by the
criminals David has taken out.

00:22:17.180 --> 00:22:20.539
At the bottom of the notebook, one says “Get
ready to get on the pain train.”

00:22:20.539 --> 00:22:23.470
David first discovers his powers by surviving
a train wreck.

00:22:23.470 --> 00:22:27.320
The one Joseph writes down about how he’s
gonna salt bae him, is a reference to this

00:22:27.320 --> 00:22:28.320
meme.

00:22:28.320 --> 00:22:31.150
If anyone was wondering, these Twitter accounts
look like they were created for the movie,

00:22:31.150 --> 00:22:35.200
then, stripped of all their content, or possibly
created after the fact to prevent anyone from

00:22:35.200 --> 00:22:37.220
pretending to be associated with the movie.

00:22:37.220 --> 00:22:41.429
The Reddit page that Joseph finds the Overseer
article on also has a link at the bottom reading:

00:22:41.429 --> 00:22:42.660
“We dead yet?”

00:22:42.660 --> 00:22:45.101
That may be a clue about the ending of the
movie.

00:22:45.101 --> 00:22:49.759
The Philly Crime Time website doesn’t actually
exist, in fact, there’s not even a .com

00:22:49.759 --> 00:22:50.759
in this URL.

00:22:50.759 --> 00:22:54.659
One of the suggested articles on the side
says: “Local citizen sees and stops assault,

00:22:54.659 --> 00:22:56.990
says Tiptoe Man inspired him to act.

00:22:56.990 --> 00:23:01.519
And then in the Four More Teens Abducted article,
it says, “some legal experts are even arguing

00:23:01.519 --> 00:23:05.399
that one personality can not be held accountable
for the actions of another, hinting at many

00:23:05.399 --> 00:23:08.480
legal obstacles ahead if the man is ever apprehended.

00:23:08.480 --> 00:23:12.740
The next day at work, M Night Shyamalan, the
director of the trilogy, makes his cameo appearance,

00:23:12.740 --> 00:23:15.440
and it answers one of the questions I had
going into the movie.

00:23:15.440 --> 00:23:19.190
He mentions that he’s getting more cameras
because one of his tenants was killed off-site.

00:23:19.190 --> 00:23:24.299
He’s talking about Dr. Fletcher, so it seems
that Jai, from Split wasn’t just an IT guy

00:23:24.299 --> 00:23:27.659
helping Dr. Fletcher review security footage,
but actually her landlord.

00:23:27.659 --> 00:23:29.530
And probably also her landlord.

00:23:29.530 --> 00:23:34.639
“You can’t use your thumbs to spin the
wheel dumb--.”

00:23:34.639 --> 00:23:38.850
Jai goes on to see David and he recognises
him as the security guard from those years

00:23:38.850 --> 00:23:42.240
ago, and tells him he used to hang out with
the shady types at the stadium, but he turned

00:23:42.240 --> 00:23:43.240
his life around.

00:23:43.240 --> 00:23:47.400
This confirms that Stadium Drug Dealer and
Jai are in fact the same character, but this

00:23:47.400 --> 00:23:51.149
is more than just a fun little director’s
cameo, it shows the effect that David had

00:23:51.149 --> 00:23:54.789
cleaning up the crime around his city; he
actually had a positive impact on the community

00:23:54.789 --> 00:23:58.690
and helped turn shady people into functioning
members of society.

00:23:58.690 --> 00:24:02.289
David goes out again to look for The Horde
with Joseph giving him tips via headphones

00:24:02.289 --> 00:24:03.690
and GPS tracker.

00:24:03.690 --> 00:24:07.730
Not only is this a common superhero trope,
but it’s also a concept that Shyamalan used

00:24:07.730 --> 00:24:11.370
in his 2013 film After Earth, although in
that movie, the roles were reversed and it

00:24:11.370 --> 00:24:13.480
was the father giving advice to his son.

00:24:13.480 --> 00:24:16.940
After David bumps into Hedwig on the street,
he heads toward the brick factory to look

00:24:16.940 --> 00:24:21.550
for the girls, and the word Allies is written
in graffiti on a window in the background,

00:24:21.550 --> 00:24:24.210
a foreshadowing the teaming up of Elijah and
The Horde.

00:24:24.210 --> 00:24:27.440
“That sounds like the bad guys teaming up.

00:24:27.440 --> 00:24:28.440
“

00:24:28.440 --> 00:24:30.529
The comic that Dr. Staple is looking at during
the final visit to the shop at the end is

00:24:30.529 --> 00:24:32.190
also called Supervillain team up.

00:24:32.190 --> 00:24:36.580
There are also huge letters spelling END,
possibly because of the twist endings to each

00:24:36.580 --> 00:24:37.580
movie.

00:24:37.580 --> 00:24:41.009
I also saw it says bender, which reminded
me of that Futurama episode where Bender and

00:24:41.009 --> 00:24:42.700
Flexo get a job in a factory.

00:24:42.700 --> 00:24:45.879
When David is first taken into Raven Hill
Memorial, the text on the top right corner

00:24:45.879 --> 00:24:50.700
of the security camera view says H20 because
David’s weakness is water and he’s about

00:24:50.700 --> 00:24:52.120
to be surrounded by it.

00:24:52.120 --> 00:24:55.919
In the Unbreakable Things You Missed, I discussed
how upside-down camera composition was used

00:24:55.919 --> 00:24:59.899
to foreshadow bad things happening, and the
trend seems to continue in Glass.

00:24:59.899 --> 00:25:02.889
When David first has the confrontation with
The Beast, we see the Beast’s point of view

00:25:02.889 --> 00:25:11.710
as he crawls along the ceiling towards David
and the rescued cheerleaders.

00:25:11.710 --> 00:25:16.039
Like many supervillains, The Beast has a signature
move, which is, fittingly, a giant bear hug.

00:25:16.039 --> 00:25:20.240
This is the same attack he used on Dr. Fletcher
during Split, on David during the factory

00:25:20.240 --> 00:25:23.450
fight and the orderly when he and Mr. Glass
are escaping.

00:25:23.450 --> 00:25:27.770
Throughout the series, broken glass is used
as a metaphor of the well being of the characters,

00:25:27.770 --> 00:25:31.049
so when David and The Beast’s battle sends
them out of the factory through a shattering

00:25:31.049 --> 00:25:35.090
glass window it spells the beginning of the
end for them, because it leads to their capture

00:25:35.090 --> 00:25:37.680
and placement in Raven Hill Memorial.

00:25:37.680 --> 00:25:41.610
Once we arrive at that institution, there
is huge clue about the final twist of the

00:25:41.610 --> 00:25:47.910
movie.

00:25:47.910 --> 00:25:51.070
As they are placed in their rooms, we are
shown the point of view of the cameras placed

00:25:51.070 --> 00:25:52.389
around the institution.

00:25:52.389 --> 00:25:56.549
The entire movie, these security camera shots
are constantly being shown, the final twist

00:25:56.549 --> 00:25:58.889
is dangled in front of us all along.

00:25:58.889 --> 00:26:02.919
The characters are introduced to their new
psychiatrist, Dr. Ellie Staple.

00:26:02.919 --> 00:26:06.180
At the end of the movie, we find out that
Dr. Staple is part of the ancient organization

00:26:06.180 --> 00:26:08.570
created to suppress superheroes from the public.

00:26:08.570 --> 00:26:12.120
When that happens, she tells Mr. Glass that
she they don’t take sides, she’s not good

00:26:12.120 --> 00:26:14.260
or evil, she essentially falls in the middle.

00:26:14.260 --> 00:26:17.950
In a literal comic book there are staples
placed in the middle crease to hold everything

00:26:17.950 --> 00:26:18.950
together.

00:26:18.950 --> 00:26:21.090
Her name represents her neutrality.

00:26:21.090 --> 00:26:25.970
The secret organisation is also something
Mr. Glass knows about way back in Unbreakable.

00:26:25.970 --> 00:26:37.250
"That's why this group, the coalition of evil,
tried to ascertain the weakness of every superhero

00:26:37.250 --> 00:26:38.250
because they all have one."

00:26:38.250 --> 00:26:39.250
They got it wrong in the comics.

00:26:39.250 --> 00:26:42.570
They talk about secret evil groups trying
to stop the heroes.

00:26:42.570 --> 00:26:47.150
I don't think we are particularly evil, and
we don't choose sides.

00:26:47.150 --> 00:26:50.500
Casey gets word of The Beast’s capture when
she’s pulled aside at school, and we also

00:26:50.500 --> 00:26:53.169
see that she attended the same school as Joseph
Dunn.

00:26:53.169 --> 00:26:56.519
I’m honestly not entirely sure what the
point of that was outside of furthering the

00:26:56.519 --> 00:27:00.330
idea that everything is connected in a comic
book story, much like how David and Clarence

00:27:00.330 --> 00:27:02.380
W Crumb were on the same train.

00:27:02.380 --> 00:27:06.201
Which, as a quick side note, Clarence’s
name continues the theme of alliteration in

00:27:06.201 --> 00:27:10.300
the first two movies with characters like
David Dunn, Casey Cooke, Kevin Crumb, and

00:27:10.300 --> 00:27:11.509
now Clarence Crumb.

00:27:11.509 --> 00:27:15.399
There’s also a character that I noticed
in the IMDb credits called Scarlet Shields…

00:27:15.399 --> 00:27:18.139
I honestly have no idea who that even is.

00:27:18.139 --> 00:27:22.139
I’m assuming she’s a minor character,
but basically every other minor character

00:27:22.139 --> 00:27:25.679
has a name like Hospital Patient or Cheerleading
Girl #4.

00:27:25.679 --> 00:27:28.419
I honestly have no idea who this is supposed
to be.

00:27:28.419 --> 00:27:31.720
Maybe she was given a name just to throw off
people trying to look up information online

00:27:31.720 --> 00:27:33.230
before the movie came out?

00:27:33.230 --> 00:27:37.770
David’s son Joseph meets with Dr. Staple
to try to convince her to let David go free.

00:27:37.770 --> 00:27:41.360
When he is unsuccessful, the camera tilts
down into an upside-down position again to

00:27:41.360 --> 00:27:43.039
watch Joseph leave the facility.

00:27:43.039 --> 00:27:47.330
Just as Joseph saw the original train crash
footage upside-down on the couch in Unbreakable,

00:27:47.330 --> 00:27:51.360
this camera movement in Glass also represents
impending disaster.

00:27:51.360 --> 00:27:55.389
Speaking of Unbreakable, when I saw the scene
of David coming into a young Joseph’s room,

00:27:55.389 --> 00:27:59.960
I was completely blown away by it, because
somehow I had no idea that these deleted scenes

00:27:59.960 --> 00:28:03.990
from the first film existed, and this one
really works well considering the themes of

00:28:03.990 --> 00:28:04.990
Glass.

00:28:04.990 --> 00:28:06.409
Let’s roll it.

00:28:06.409 --> 00:28:10.360
“I’m not scared.”

00:28:10.360 --> 00:28:12.990
“That’s great.”

00:28:12.990 --> 00:28:16.930
“You know why?

00:28:16.930 --> 00:28:20.880
I know now.”

00:28:20.880 --> 00:28:23.510
“Know what?”

00:28:23.510 --> 00:28:27.460
“Your secret identity.”

00:28:27.460 --> 00:28:32.370
So Joseph felt uneasy about the fact that
his father has these incredible abilities

00:28:32.370 --> 00:28:36.840
that can’t be explained, but finds comfort
in knowing he has someone to protect him.

00:28:36.840 --> 00:28:40.640
This helps explain why it was so important
for Mr. Glass to outsmart the black clover

00:28:40.640 --> 00:28:44.669
society and broadcast the existence of superheroes
out to the world.

00:28:44.669 --> 00:28:48.320
Next, Casey is given the opportunity to meet
with The Horde, and discovers that her touch

00:28:48.320 --> 00:28:50.470
can bring Kevin forward into the light.

00:28:50.470 --> 00:28:54.350
My theory as to why Casey has this ability
relates to the fact that the additional identities

00:28:54.350 --> 00:28:58.289
were created by Kevin’s brain as a coping
mechanism for the abuse dished out by his

00:28:58.289 --> 00:28:59.289
mother.

00:28:59.289 --> 00:29:01.929
It’s stated in Split that the Horde exists
to protect Kevin,

00:29:01.929 --> 00:29:03.669
“Are you in charge?”

00:29:03.669 --> 00:29:05.460
“Yeah, we’ve taken charge.

00:29:05.460 --> 00:29:08.120
We’re the only ones that can protect Kevin.”

00:29:08.120 --> 00:29:09.749
“We’re all here to protect Kevin.”

00:29:09.749 --> 00:29:12.039
“He’s very weak.”

00:29:12.039 --> 00:29:16.980
So naturally, the way to bring down these
protections is with love and kindness.

00:29:16.980 --> 00:29:20.929
Casey is the only one who’s capable of this
because she too has been abused by her Uncle,

00:29:20.929 --> 00:29:24.350
so she knows what kind of gentle hand is needed
to undo the damage.

00:29:24.350 --> 00:29:27.669
When Casey leaves the institution after that,
she puts on the jacket given to her by the

00:29:27.669 --> 00:29:31.929
man working at the Philadelphia Zoo who escorts
her out of danger at the end of Split.

00:29:31.929 --> 00:29:35.710
My guess is that she still wears that jacket
as a reminder of how she stood up to The Beast

00:29:35.710 --> 00:29:39.809
-- something that also gave her the strength
to stand up to her Uncle, and just to be a

00:29:39.809 --> 00:29:41.620
stronger, braver person overall.

00:29:41.620 --> 00:29:45.950
In the final examination scene, Dr. Staple
tries to convince Mr. Glass, The Horde and

00:29:45.950 --> 00:29:50.110
The Overseer that they don’t actually have
super powers by giving rational explanations

00:29:50.110 --> 00:29:53.970
for everything that has happened and telling
them they will remain institutionalized for

00:29:53.970 --> 00:29:57.530
the rest of their lives if they are unable
to overcome their “disorder”.

00:29:57.530 --> 00:30:01.350
In a way, she is actually telling the truth
-- although we don’t know it yet, the black

00:30:01.350 --> 00:30:05.720
clover society was planning to kill them if
Dr. Staple didn’t successfully convince

00:30:05.720 --> 00:30:07.980
them they are ordinary in the three day timespan.

00:30:07.980 --> 00:30:11.360
But I’ll get back to the black clover society
later in this video.

00:30:11.360 --> 00:30:15.970
Dr. Staple tells David he has symptoms of
the supposed superhero disorder, but lacks

00:30:15.970 --> 00:30:19.610
some kind of anchoring incident that made
him realize that he is a superhero, which

00:30:19.610 --> 00:30:24.000
is funny because the “anchoring incident”
he thinks of is literally him drowning like

00:30:24.000 --> 00:30:25.000
an anchor.

00:30:25.000 --> 00:30:28.290
One of the main talking points that Dr. Staple
uses to try to convince them that they are

00:30:28.290 --> 00:30:32.389
ordinary, is that if superheroes do exist,
why would there only be the three of them?

00:30:32.389 --> 00:30:37.120
This is Dr. Staple counting on the fact that
her black clover society will always be successful

00:30:37.120 --> 00:30:39.669
in suppressing any supers from the public
eye.

00:30:39.669 --> 00:30:43.220
David and Patricia appear to have their faith
in their own powers shaken.

00:30:43.220 --> 00:30:47.100
Elijah, doesn’t respond, because he’s
pretending to be a vegetable, but he knows

00:30:47.100 --> 00:30:55.019
that Dr. Staple is lying to them.

00:30:55.019 --> 00:30:59.100
All the talk of comic books sends Casey to
the comic-book store to do some of her own

00:30:59.100 --> 00:31:04.249
research, and the store is owned by none other
than the comic book store clerk from Unbreakable.

00:31:04.249 --> 00:31:08.169
It seems that his suspicions of pervs in back
of the store hasn’t changed either, when

00:31:08.169 --> 00:31:11.659
he yells to Joseph, “you better not be one
of those Hello Kitty pervs.”

00:31:11.659 --> 00:31:18.899
“You better not be jacking off to the Japanese
comics I swear to God.”

00:31:18.899 --> 00:31:22.700
In the background there’s a comic titled
"Strange Happenings" which is possibly a nod

00:31:22.700 --> 00:31:27.759
to M. Night's 2008 film "The Happening", and
as Joseph leaves the store, he notices a comic

00:31:27.759 --> 00:31:31.200
book called "Whisperman", which has been made
specifically for this movie.

00:31:31.200 --> 00:31:35.539
The artist has a YouTube Channel, where he
calls the character a puppet-master of sorts,

00:31:35.539 --> 00:31:39.830
which reminds me of Dr Staple’s attempt
to manipulate the heroes into thinking they’re

00:31:39.830 --> 00:31:40.830
ordinary.

00:31:40.830 --> 00:31:45.070
Shortly after, he does some research on Kevin
Crumb, and the author of one of the articles

00:31:45.070 --> 00:31:49.059
is Matthew Shapiro, one of the guys who emailed
Dr. Fletcher in Split.

00:31:49.059 --> 00:31:52.840
When Mr. Glass looks at Kevin’s file, if
you pause you can discover that Kevin’s

00:31:52.840 --> 00:31:54.539
mother also had DID.

00:31:54.539 --> 00:31:56.840
It says “Mother unfit for child custody.

00:31:56.840 --> 00:32:01.460
Mother’s mental illness (DID) may have a
profound effect on her child’s development,

00:32:01.460 --> 00:32:04.500
including an increased risk of the child developing
the same disorder.”

00:32:04.500 --> 00:32:09.309
So when his father was on Eastrail 177, he
was seeking help for his wife at the time,

00:32:09.309 --> 00:32:10.639
not his son.

00:32:10.639 --> 00:32:14.549
Just as the mirror reflection shots are used
to introduce villains in Unbreakable and Split,

00:32:14.549 --> 00:32:18.279
similar shots are used in Glass to show that
something is not right.

00:32:18.279 --> 00:32:22.159
David sits on floor of his cell and his reflection
is distorted by the curved wall.

00:32:22.159 --> 00:32:26.419
It is shortly after this that we discover
Elijah was faking his sedation and has the

00:32:26.419 --> 00:32:30.999
ability to sneak out of his room and he discovers
the magazine advertising the opening of Osaka

00:32:30.999 --> 00:32:31.999
Tower.

00:32:31.999 --> 00:32:35.950
Just as the previous movies had subtle references
to The Fantastic Four and Teen Titans, the

00:32:35.950 --> 00:32:39.490
headline of this article calls Osaka Tower
a true MARVEL.

00:32:39.490 --> 00:32:44.440
Also, in a look-in at the Osaka Tower article
I saw the photography was done by Dave Kellom,

00:32:44.440 --> 00:32:46.830
an art department coordinator on Glass.

00:32:46.830 --> 00:32:50.940
Elijah tells The Beast that his plan is to
attack the tower on its opening date, December

00:32:50.940 --> 00:32:54.460
7th, which is Pearl Harbor Day another major
American disaster.

00:32:54.460 --> 00:33:00.049
More importantly, that’s also my birthday,
so put that down in your calendar right now.

00:33:00.049 --> 00:33:01.919
Right now.

00:33:01.919 --> 00:33:05.749
Then we get a glimpse into Elijah’s past,
when he sneaks onto a carnival ride and tries

00:33:05.749 --> 00:33:07.440
to protect himself using stuffed animals.

00:33:07.440 --> 00:33:10.210
This is another deleted scene, but again,
it works really well here because The Beast

00:33:10.210 --> 00:33:14.370
ends protecting him from the orderlies and
the police as they break out of the hospital,

00:33:14.370 --> 00:33:17.740
so it’s kind of as if he’s been protected
by animals every step of the way.

00:33:17.740 --> 00:33:21.549
It’s also interesting to note that his plan
on the carnival ride backfires, and he ends

00:33:21.549 --> 00:33:25.879
up breaking his shoulder, just as The Beast
turns on him at the end of Glass and breaks

00:33:25.879 --> 00:33:28.350
his shoulder, an injury he would never overcome.

00:33:28.350 --> 00:33:32.009
After Elijah discovers the powers of The Beast,
he formulates his plan to have The Beast battle

00:33:32.009 --> 00:33:33.240
David in front of the world.

00:33:33.240 --> 00:33:36.759
I think it’s important to note that it was
never Mr. Glass’s real intention to go to

00:33:36.759 --> 00:33:40.350
the tower, all he really needed to do was
convince The Beast to break them out so he

00:33:40.350 --> 00:33:42.269
could stream it using the cameras.

00:33:42.269 --> 00:33:45.409
And for anyone who felt that David Dunn’s
part in all of this was a little underwhelming,

00:33:45.409 --> 00:33:49.270
let’s not forget that it was most likely
Dunn’s security company who provides all

00:33:49.270 --> 00:33:52.070
the cameras to the institution in the first
place.

00:33:52.070 --> 00:33:55.690
Part of Elijah’s plan was to change out
the lens of the machine used for his surgery,

00:33:55.690 --> 00:33:59.649
then get himself caught lollygagging around
on camera so that the doctor moves up the

00:33:59.649 --> 00:34:00.909
date of his operation.

00:34:00.909 --> 00:34:04.960
This is important because it allows the orderly,
Daryl, to let his guard down around Elijah,

00:34:04.960 --> 00:34:08.700
giving him the opportunity to slit his throat
with the broken shard of glass.

00:34:08.700 --> 00:34:13.730
And just as Elijah’s broken glass cane represented
his injuries in Unbreakable, the broken picture

00:34:13.730 --> 00:34:16.800
frames foreshadow his eventual demise in Glass.

00:34:16.800 --> 00:34:19.670
All three characters have their “broken
glass moment”.

00:34:19.670 --> 00:34:23.240
At the end of the second act there are a couple
more clever uses of shots that use mirror

00:34:23.240 --> 00:34:24.710
reflections to tell us something.

00:34:24.710 --> 00:34:28.540
The first is Dr. Staple getting out of her
car and heading into Raven Hill Memorial,

00:34:28.540 --> 00:34:30.110
which we see through her side mirror.

00:34:30.110 --> 00:34:34.170
These mirrors always come with a disclaimer:
objects in mirror are closer than they appear.

00:34:34.170 --> 00:34:38.310
Well, Dr. Staple is not just a psychiatrist
as she appears to be, because she’s actually

00:34:38.310 --> 00:34:40.150
part of this secret organization.

00:34:40.150 --> 00:34:43.900
Our earlier mirror shots of David and The
Horde are distorted by curved mirrors, but

00:34:43.900 --> 00:34:47.850
when Elijah finally meets The Beast, he first
sees the transformation through the reflection

00:34:47.850 --> 00:34:49.450
of a glass cabinet.

00:34:49.450 --> 00:34:52.440
And there’s no distortion here, which tells
us that things are going to be essentially

00:34:52.440 --> 00:34:55.820
as they should be with the impending clash
of good vs. evil.

00:34:55.820 --> 00:35:00.510
When Dr. Staple realizes that Elijah has broken
out, she sees the news report on TV about

00:35:00.510 --> 00:35:04.350
the opening of Osaka Tower, and thinks Mr.
Glass is going to sabotage it.

00:35:04.350 --> 00:35:08.360
Also, the reporter is the same guy who reports
on the missing girls in Split, and on the

00:35:08.360 --> 00:35:10.810
news ticker at the bottom, there is a report
about cryptocurrency.

00:35:10.810 --> 00:35:15.390
Krypton is the name of Superman’s home planet,
and Superman is referenced several times throughout

00:35:15.390 --> 00:35:16.390
Glass.

00:35:16.390 --> 00:35:20.430
Shortly after, the final battle begins, and
Dr. Staple curiously tells someone to make

00:35:20.430 --> 00:35:23.520
sure to keep patients and staff away from
the south side windows.

00:35:23.520 --> 00:35:27.580
This is because she knows that David, Elijah
and Kevin’s powers are real, and it’s

00:35:27.580 --> 00:35:29.770
her duty to make sure nobody finds out about
them.

00:35:29.770 --> 00:35:32.950
So that brings us back to this whole black
clover society.

00:35:32.950 --> 00:35:33.950
Who are they?

00:35:33.950 --> 00:35:35.230
Where did they come from?

00:35:35.230 --> 00:35:37.370
Why do they have these matching tattoos?

00:35:37.370 --> 00:35:40.280
And what do they have to do with Split and
Unbreakable?

00:35:40.280 --> 00:35:47.680
The answers to all of these questions are
coming up.

00:35:47.680 --> 00:35:51.640
At the end of the confrontation, a mysterious
group of SWAT members all sharing a wrist

00:35:51.640 --> 00:35:55.910
tattoo of black three leaf clover show up
to kill David and The Beast.

00:35:55.910 --> 00:35:58.630
Dr. Staple is revealed to be a part of this
society.

00:35:58.630 --> 00:36:02.520
She explains that they are a group that has
been around for 10,000 years to keep superheroes

00:36:02.520 --> 00:36:06.750
out of the public eye, because it’s not
fair to the rest of society to have Gods walking

00:36:06.750 --> 00:36:07.750
among us.

00:36:07.750 --> 00:36:11.580
Dr. Staple’s mission the entire time was
to get them to believe that their powers weren’t

00:36:11.580 --> 00:36:14.130
real so they can go on living ordinary lives.

00:36:14.130 --> 00:36:18.210
She was given the three days to do so, but
if she failed, the alternative was some kind

00:36:18.210 --> 00:36:20.190
of brain surgery, or death.

00:36:20.190 --> 00:36:24.940
In Split, we are shown how the organization’s
manipulation of society has worked.

00:36:24.940 --> 00:36:29.140
Society sees The Horde’s dissociative identity
disorder as a problem, a mental illness that

00:36:29.140 --> 00:36:30.200
needs to be cured.

00:36:30.200 --> 00:36:34.580
Dr. Fletcher’s thesis to the medical community
is that maybe those with this condition are

00:36:34.580 --> 00:36:37.030
actually extraordinarily gifted.

00:36:37.030 --> 00:36:43.840
“Well, we look at people who are shattered
and different as less than.

00:36:43.840 --> 00:36:48.120
But what if they are more than us?”

00:36:48.120 --> 00:36:52.770
But Dr. Fletcher is largely rejected by her
peers, and it’s because the black clover

00:36:52.770 --> 00:36:57.600
society has been working for 10,000 years
to condition us to see this as a mental illness.

00:36:57.600 --> 00:37:02.240
That’s exactly what Dr. Staple does in Glass,
she rounds up three of the most extraordinary

00:37:02.240 --> 00:37:06.450
supers in Philadelphia and tries to convince
them that something is wrong with them and

00:37:06.450 --> 00:37:07.510
that they need treatment.

00:37:07.510 --> 00:37:11.250
That’s why she wants Casey to get Kevin
to hold onto the light, because she is aware

00:37:11.250 --> 00:37:13.970
of the power someone with DID is capable of.

00:37:13.970 --> 00:37:17.860
The existence of this group also explains
a question brought up way back when Elijah

00:37:17.860 --> 00:37:20.370
and David have their first meeting in Unbreakable.

00:37:20.370 --> 00:37:26.350
“I believe comics are our last link to an
ancient way of passing on history.

00:37:26.350 --> 00:37:28.910
The Egyptians drew on walls.

00:37:28.910 --> 00:37:33.120
Countries all over the world still pass on
knowledge through pictorial forms.”

00:37:33.120 --> 00:37:36.850
Remember when Dr. Staple is meeting with Joseph,
Casey and Elijah’s mother, and tries to

00:37:36.850 --> 00:37:39.400
convince them that comics are nothing more
than fantasy?

00:37:39.400 --> 00:37:42.670
She even brings up comic-book conventions
to try to invalidate them.

00:37:42.670 --> 00:37:46.510
The only time she gets frustrated is when
they try to link their situation to what they

00:37:46.510 --> 00:37:47.620
have seen in comic books.

00:37:47.620 --> 00:37:51.800
The clover society is there to ensure that
these stories exist through pictures, as seemingly

00:37:51.800 --> 00:37:53.610
fictional stories, but nothing more.

00:37:53.610 --> 00:37:59.320
“I believe comics are a form of history
that someone somewhere felt or experienced.

00:37:59.320 --> 00:38:03.720
Then of course those experiences and that
history got chewed up in the commercial machine,

00:38:03.720 --> 00:38:08.010
got jazzed up, made into titillating cartoons
for the sale rack.”

00:38:08.010 --> 00:38:12.580
In Glass, the “someone somewhere” Elijah
is referring to is his mother, Joseph and

00:38:12.580 --> 00:38:17.230
Casey, only this time instead of distributing
comics to be chewed up in the commercial machine,

00:38:17.230 --> 00:38:20.870
they have actual video evidence of the existence
of these powers.

00:38:20.870 --> 00:38:25.480
Dr. Staple also mentions that when one super
appears, another is likely to appear opposite

00:38:25.480 --> 00:38:29.330
of him, and it just leads to conflict, which
is why she feels the clover society needs

00:38:29.330 --> 00:38:30.790
to appear to pacify them.

00:38:30.790 --> 00:38:35.530
“If there is someone like me in the world
and I am at one end of the spectrum, couldn’t

00:38:35.530 --> 00:38:39.730
there be someone else opposite of me at the
other end.

00:38:39.730 --> 00:38:44.850
Someone who doesn’t get sick, who doesn’t
get hurt like the rest of us.

00:38:44.850 --> 00:38:48.650
And he probably doesn’t even know it.”

00:38:48.650 --> 00:38:52.700
OK, but why the black clover tattoos, that
seems kind of random?

00:38:52.700 --> 00:38:53.710
Well maybe not.

00:38:53.710 --> 00:38:58.760
We can look at it from the secret organization’s
perspective and from a filmmaking perspective.

00:38:58.760 --> 00:39:00.380
First from a filmmaking perspective.

00:39:00.380 --> 00:39:04.140
The fact that David, Elijah and The Horde’s
journey as superpowered humans ends with a

00:39:04.140 --> 00:39:07.250
tattoo of these clovers kind of brings the
trilogy full circle.

00:39:07.250 --> 00:39:10.700
Let’s go wayyy back to when we are introduced
to David in Unbreakable.

00:39:10.700 --> 00:39:15.120
A woman appears asking him if he’s alone,
and she takes the spot next to him on the

00:39:15.120 --> 00:39:16.120
train.

00:39:16.120 --> 00:39:19.960
He notices a tattoo on her abdomen which appears
to be a rose, but we only see the bottom of

00:39:19.960 --> 00:39:22.830
the stem because this is the very root of
David’s story.

00:39:22.830 --> 00:39:26.200
When we see the secret society’s clover
tattoos at the very end of David’s story,

00:39:26.200 --> 00:39:30.060
we’re seeing the top of the plant, so it's
as if we’ve come all the way around.

00:39:30.060 --> 00:39:33.420
But then why not use a rose tattoo for the
society as well?

00:39:33.420 --> 00:39:36.080
The clover does a better job of representing
their values.

00:39:36.080 --> 00:39:39.960
They essentially want to purge the world of
anyone who has these rare, special powers.

00:39:39.960 --> 00:39:44.180
A four leaf clover is considered a rare and
lucky find, much like how a superhero is a

00:39:44.180 --> 00:39:46.110
rare incredible standout in our society.

00:39:46.110 --> 00:39:50.510
But the black clover people don’t want that,
they want everyone to be a three leaf clover

00:39:50.510 --> 00:39:53.820
and that’s why is was chosen as the symbol
of their organization.

00:39:53.820 --> 00:39:57.490
Finally, there was one other minute detail
that I felt really brought the series to a

00:39:57.490 --> 00:39:58.750
nice conclusion.

00:39:58.750 --> 00:40:03.130
Mr. Glass famously gets his supervillain name
from the kids that made fun of his condition,

00:40:03.130 --> 00:40:04.130
osteogenesis imperfecta.

00:40:04.130 --> 00:40:06.330
“They called me Mr. Glass.”

00:40:06.330 --> 00:40:10.820
Elijah’s mother lives across from a playground,
we see this in a flashback during Unbreakable.

00:40:10.820 --> 00:40:14.560
At the end of Glass, before the email comes
in from Elijah containing the footage of the

00:40:14.560 --> 00:40:18.030
final battle, you can hear the sounds of children
playing from outside.

00:40:18.030 --> 00:40:21.990
How fitting that the very playground with
the kids that poked fun at Elijah, part of

00:40:21.990 --> 00:40:26.500
what put the villain idea in his head and
gave him his awakening as a supervillain can

00:40:26.500 --> 00:40:30.800
be heard again, just before Elijah’s mother
puts out that video to help all heroes and

00:40:30.800 --> 00:40:34.360
villains across the world have their realization
and awakening.

00:40:34.360 --> 00:40:38.460
When David first accepts his newfound powers
in Unbreakable, Elijah tells him to go to

00:40:38.460 --> 00:40:40.860
where there are people, and he goes to the
train station.

00:40:40.860 --> 00:40:45.570
That’s exactly what Mrs. Price, Joseph and
Casey do when they unveil the existence of

00:40:45.570 --> 00:40:54.150
these comic book heroes to the world.

00:40:54.150 --> 00:40:59.040
